# T-1015: Documentation test — Color unit constructors evaluate correctly at runtime.
# Color: [type Red Green Blue] injects Red, Green, Blue as qualified Variant entries.
# TypeAlias entry Color is skipped at runtime. result: Green references the injected
# Green constructor (Variant(Color.Green, Null)).
# NOTE: T-1015 originally called for a type error when the wrong variant is assigned to
# a typed-Color slot (e.g. passing Red where only Green or Blue is accepted). That scenario
# requires cross-scope TyCon identity enforcement, which is deferred to B-343. Until B-343,
# the type checker cannot distinguish Color.Red from Color.Green by TyCon nominal identity.
# This test therefore documents that unit constructors from [type] declarations evaluate to
# Variant values; the actual type-error path will be covered by a new test in B-343.
[
  Color: [type Red Green Blue]
  result: Green
]
=== out
Dict({"Red": Variant(Color.Red, Null), "Green": Variant(Color.Green, Null), "Blue": Variant(Color.Blue, Null), "Color": Dict({"Red": Variant(Color.Red, Null), "Green": Variant(Color.Green, Null), "Blue": Variant(Color.Blue, Null)}), "result": Variant(Color.Green, Null)})
